WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.194
Today is November 10, 2026.

3
00:00:07.194 --> 00:00:13.211
Overnight, Wall Street staged a powerful broad based rally driven by massive short covering.

4
00:00:13.211 --> 00:00:20.760
The Nasdaq surged 2.74 percent, while the S and P 500 climbed 2.35 percent.

5
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:26.643
The Dow Jones Industrial Average also advanced 2.15 percent across the board.

6
00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:32.844
Diplomatic talks between Washington and Tehran mediated by Qatar sparked the initial relief rally.

7
00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:40.307
Rumored framework terms include a 3.67 percent uranium enrichment cap and reopening the Strait of Hormuz.

8
00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:46.557
Washington would also unfreeze between 6 billion and 9 billion dollars in Iranian assets.

9
00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:52.611
Crude oil plunged on the news, pulling ten year and thirty year Treasury yields sharply lower.

10
00:00:52.611 --> 00:01:00.000
The volatility index tumbled, reversing forced selling from volatility control funds and lifting equity futures.

11
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.349
However, market veterans warn that Middle East headlines often serve as institutional smoke screens.

12
00:01:06.349 --> 00:01:12.488
This single day rebound requires three to five trading days of follow through to confirm a reversal.

13
00:01:12.488 --> 00:01:19.032
Today's October consumer price index report will dictate the Federal Reserve rate path and market direction.

14
00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:26.263
Technically, the Nasdaq 100 reclaimed its 50 week moving average, signaling a potential bottoming reversal.

15
00:01:26.263 --> 00:01:32.402
Bulls need a Friday close above both the 5 week and 50 week averages to confirm upside.

16
00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:39.584
Until the Nasdaq 100 reclaims 29000, a secondary retest of recent lows remains possible.

17
00:01:39.584 --> 00:01:46.557
Triple Q closed below 680 dollars and faces heavy overhead resistance at 700 dollars.

18
00:01:46.557 --> 00:01:53.505
The S and P 500 must break through major resistance at 7600 to reclaim its upper range.

19
00:01:53.505 --> 00:02:01.177
Meanwhile, the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index filled its November 5 gap, facing key resistance near 1900.

20
00:02:01.177 --> 00:02:07.782
Falling yields and deep valuation resets are reshaping technology and semiconductor capital flows.

21
00:02:07.782 --> 00:02:14.302
The S and P 500 tech sector forward price to earnings ratio has fallen to 17 times.

22
00:02:14.302 --> 00:02:20.564
Tech now trades below the broader market's 18 multiple for the first time since 2017.

23
00:02:20.564 --> 00:02:26.300
That marks a dramatic compression from the 32 multiple reached in October 2025.

24
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:33.309
Goldman Sachs compares this correction to the 1998 liquidity crisis rather than the 2000 dot com bust.

25
00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:40.037
Forced deleveraging drove the recent pullback, while underlying artificial intelligence demand remains intact.

26
00:02:40.037 --> 00:02:46.765
Still, private market valuations are undergoing a reality check as investors demand real cash flow.

27
00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:53.959
Anthropic slashed its valuation target by 40 percent to 1.2 trillion dollars ahead of next week's IPO.

28
00:02:53.959 --> 00:03:01.716
OpenAI similarly trimmed its valuation target from 1.5 trillion down to 1.25 trillion dollars.

29
00:03:01.716 --> 00:03:09.192
As long as Microsoft and Google maintain strong cloud capital expenditures, hardware supply chains remain safe.

30
00:03:09.192 --> 00:03:16.557
Within semiconductors, sudden governance turmoil at Nvidia triggered violent capital rotation across chipmakers.

31
00:03:16.557 --> 00:03:23.444
Nvidia fell against the rally amid probe rumors linking CEO Jensen Huang's contact to chip smuggling.

32
00:03:23.444 --> 00:03:30.969
Investigators suspect a Singapore front company scheme to divert graphics cards rather than core technology espionage.

33
00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:38.996
With Nvidia facing November 17 earnings and a November 18 congressional hearing, institutions rotated into rivals.

34
00:03:38.996 --> 00:03:45.809
Meanwhile, Google lagged with a 1.18 percent gain as its new tensor chips failed to impress.

35
00:03:45.944 --> 00:03:52.168
Among actionable equities, A M D stands out as the premier semiconductor safe haven buy.

36
00:03:52.118 --> 00:04:00.035
Shares surged 13.26 percent as institutional capital fled Nvidia governance risk for Lisa Su's leadership.

37
00:04:00.035 --> 00:04:06.812
Backed by strong recent earnings and Wall Street upgrades, A M D offers an actionable buy on dips.

38
00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:14.128
Broadcom also captured spillover inflows, though A M D carries cleaner management certainty into mid November.

39
00:04:14.128 --> 00:04:21.493
Optical communications leader Coherent, ticker C O H R, also triggers an actionable rebound buy signal.

40
00:04:21.493 --> 00:04:27.339
Following the Lumentum and Marvell merger, Coherent is taking over as the optical sector leader.

41
00:04:27.339 --> 00:04:36.260
A 62 percent drawdown purged valuation froth, setting a profit taking target between 250 and 260 dollars.

42
00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:43.466
Nuclear power leader Constellation Energy, ticker C E G, flashes a strong fundamental buy signal.

43
00:04:43.466 --> 00:04:52.645
Third quarter revenue jumped 45 percent to 9.55 billion dollars, while net income doubled to 1.84 billion dollars.

44
00:04:52.645 --> 00:05:00.071
Driven by favorable power pricing and the Calpine acquisition, management raised 2026 guidance a second time.

45
00:05:00.071 --> 00:05:06.652
Traders can buy breakouts above the one year moving average, targeting the 250 day moving average.

46
00:05:06.652 --> 00:05:13.233
Berkshire Hathaway, ticker B R K, offers an actionable value accumulation buy on pullbacks.

47
00:05:13.233 --> 00:05:20.022
Nine month operating earnings grew 8 percent as rail and manufacturing offset softer insurance underwriting.

48
00:05:20.022 --> 00:05:28.098
Record cash of 377 billion dollars and 9.6 billion dollars in buybacks signal deep intrinsic value.

49
00:05:28.098 --> 00:05:35.108
With Wall Street stabilizing sentiment ahead of Anthropic's IPO next week, traders should scale in on dips.

50
00:05:35.108 --> 00:05:40.635
Keep position sizes disciplined and use Monday's lows as strict stop loss levels.

51
00:05:40.635 --> 00:05:44.643
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

52
00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:48.809
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
